cards.content:
`Stream.of(...)` berguna kalau datanya belum ada di list:

```java
Stream<String> hari = Stream.of("Senin", "Selasa", "Rabu");
```

`Arrays.stream(...)` membuat Stream dari array. Untuk array `int[]`, hasilnya adalah **IntStream**, Stream khusus angka yang punya method tambahan seperti `sum()`:

```java run
import java.util.Arrays;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] belanja = {15000, 8000, 22000};
        int total = Arrays.stream(belanja).sum();
        System.out.println("Total: " + total);
    }
}
```

Semua kelas Stream ada di paket `java.util.stream`: `Stream`, `IntStream`, dan `Collectors`.

cards.code:
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;
import java.util.stream.IntStream;
import java.util.stream.Stream;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<String> buah = Arrays.asList("apel", "mangga", "jeruk");
        System.out.println(buah.stream().count());

        Stream<String> hari = Stream.of("Senin", "Selasa", "Rabu");
        System.out.println(hari.collect(Collectors.toList()));

        int[] skor = {7, 9, 4};
        System.out.println(Arrays.stream(skor).sum());

        System.out.println(IntStream.range(1, 5).sum());
        System.out.println(IntStream.rangeClosed(1, 5).sum());
    }
}

